  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Replacement of lost livelihoods assets for most affected households following 2011 floods - ADD</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Exceptionally heavy monsoon rain from late July to August 2012 affected or damaged crops, fish/shrimp/crab ponds, other household assets and income generation activities. Approximately 4,277 households of the &#x2018;Improved Food and Livelihood Security&#x2019; (IFLS) programme beneficiaries in Bagerhat district, Bangladesh were affected. 

This grant will support ADD in responding to the needs of the IFLS beneficiaries who lost their livelihoods assets, and whose households were made severely vulnerable owing to the floods. The response is taking into account the recommendations from the mid-term review of the IFLS programme, which was undertaken in December 2011.</narrative>
  </description>
